{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 94,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, show thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render a reward to the proud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall they utter ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " speak hard things? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all the workers of iniquity boast themselves?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They break in pieces thy people, O LORD, and afflict thy heritage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet they say, The LORD will not see, neither will the God of Jacob regard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Understand, ye brutish among the people: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fools, when will ye be wise?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that chastiseth the heathen, shall he not correct? he that teacheth man knowledge, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall he not know",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD knoweth the thoughts of man, that they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the man whom thou chastenest, O LORD, and teachest him out of thy law;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the LORD will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But judgment shall return to righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who will rise up for me against the evil-doers? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Unless the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my help, my soul had almost dwelt in silence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O LORD, held me up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the multitude of my thoughts within me, thy comforts delight my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by a law?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They assemble themselves against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the LORD is my defense; and my God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rock of my refuge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.94.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.94.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he will bring upon them their own iniquity, and will cut them off in their own wickedness; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the LORD our God will cut them off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
